# Debugging

- Trace the current Workspace entry point, owner, transport, and store before forming a fix. Legacy helpers with similar names may be unrelated.
- Separate observed behavior, source evidence, hypotheses, and reproduction gaps.
- Use existing scoped logging and diagnostics; do not log credentials, message bodies, or raw storage dumps.
- Reduce the failure to the smallest relevant scenario. Check organization/project changes, delayed responses, cached state, and reconnect when the symptom involves stale data.
- For memory growth, compare retained heap after cleanup/GC with temporary allocation peaks. For rendering cost, measure actual rerenders before adding memoization.
- Analysis-only requests do not authorize code changes.
